# TensorFold native 1.0.7 (Ash Hart), Nemotron 3.5 Lightning 30B-A3B, one DGX Station: RTX PRO 6000 vs GB300 (sm_103)
# 2026-10-11 PT. Excerpt of the run log, per-request bench summaries, smoke check and Ash's tf-cuda-test on the GB300 (scrubbed).
# N6 = RTX PRO 6000, Ash's release archive tensorfold-1.0.7-linux-aarch64.tar.gz (sha256 1bc88821...), MLX 4-bit checkpoint.
# G4 / GF = GB300, our sm_103 build of 1.0.7 source e7c523eb: zig 0.17.0, in nvcr.io/nvidia/pytorch:26.07-py3:
#   zig build -Dnvcc=/usr/local/cuda/bin/nvcc -Dsm=103 -Doptimize=fast native   -> tensorfold-native (sha256 8d9be885...)
#   G4 = MLX 4-bit checkpoint, GF = NVIDIA NVFP4 checkpoint.
# Server (Ash's runbook): tensorfold-native serve MODEL --parallel 1 --context 40960 --temperature 0 --no-thinking, one GPU, --network none.
# Bench: prose prompts, fresh seeds; decode = mean of per-request decode tok/s over 5 requests per rep; C1 x3 reps; C4 queued (--parallel 1).
# The first GB300 attempt (18:38) used the CLI binary (no serve) and failed 'unknown option --name'; the arms below are the 19:45 re-run.

